[Applause]  dawn breaking in london and the labour  mayor in good spirits  the capitals council's changing hands  labour winning here in wandsworth a  symbolic success for the party  and the outgoing conservative leader  clear national issues at play the cost  of living is a bit of an issue and  people are complaining about that there  have been other comments about what is  happening nationally which is affecting  people's judgment and people are making  that judgment between national and local  and casting their vote as they want to  partygate also spoiling the mood for  conservative councillors in westminster  another tory council fall into labour  for the first time  ever  jubilation for him  here in barnet to hug in the handover of  a third tory council this is a big  turning point for us from the depths of  2019 that general election  back on track that change this last two  years has been really hard for us as a  party but we've done it we've built  those solid foundations  solid strides and fresh foundations in  southern england perhaps more troubling  for boris johnson the liberal democrats  finally regaining ground  from the tory heartlands of west  oxfordshire to south west england in the  town of taunton i wasn't expecting that  the lib dems exceeding expectations  what began as a tremor  in cheshire  became a earthquake in north shropshire  with our victories  in westmoreland and furnace  and our victories here in somerset  it's now become a political shock wave  that could bring down this appalling  conservative government  i might go it looks a bit greener  that not the picture this pm would paint  of this set of election results by no  means the royal reception you received  at last year's elections but this not a  total catastrophe either she is the  longest serving  monarch  in the history of the country boris  johnson dismissing symbolic losses and  minor gains as mid-term blues  it's midterm and it's certainly a mixed  set of results and  we've had a tough night in some parts of  the of the country but on the other hand  in other parts of the country you're  still seeing uh conservatives going  forward and  making uh quite remarkable gains the big  lesson that i take from this is that  this is a message from voters that what  they want us to do above all one two and  three is focus on the big issues that  matter to them but just down the road  from the pm on this visit to his  constituency his own mp say partygate  very much did matter it's very clear on  doorsteps there is a message here people  have switched their votes to lots of  different other parties they haven't  endorsed labor endorse the liberal  democrats of the greens but they are  clearly sending a message to my party to  the government that i support to say  that there needs to be some change  across london the day didn't start well  for the prime minister from wandsworth  to here in westminster the tory party  losing crucial ground in london number  10 predicted it was going to be a  grizzly night but in this fast ballot  box test for the prime minister since  the party scandal broke he emerged  battered but not entirely broken holding  enough ground in the red wall to hold  off his critics for now  this man the tory's scottish leader was  for a while one of his critics now back  behind the prime minister but behind in  the polls too the scottish tour is now  in a sore third place in scotland losing  more than 60 councillors across the  country as labour moved to second place  i aspire for us to be  in first place that's a long road ahead  i'm really pleased we're demonstrating  real progress over the course of the  last year that's been borne out by these  results where we've made gains yes from  the conservatives but we've also gained  seats from the snp we've won in places  we haven't won in for a very very long  time so a good day for the scottish  labour party but i want us to drive  forward  from scotland to the south and to london  these are bad set of results for boris  johnson but they could prove the least  of his worries as a recession and  double-digit inflation looms

